[gendo.ai](https://www.gendo.ai/resources/learn/edit-tool?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

The Canvas is the main user-facing workspace. Users should be able to upload an existing render, select an architectural element, describe a modification, attach reference images, and generate a revised version while preserving the remaining design.

### **Canvas editing workflow**

1. **Upload or generate an image.** Accept PNG, JPEG, WebP, rendered 3D views, and compatible depth/normal maps.
2. **Select the edit area.** Use brush, polygon, bounding box, click-to-segment, or text-based object selection.
3. **Refine the mask.** Add/subtract selections, feather edges, expand/shrink masks, and protect objects.
4. **Annotate the required change.** Draw arrows, sketch outlines, pin notes, and assign specific instructions to regions.
5. **Attach reference images.** Specify which reference controls the material, architectural style, furniture, lighting, or composition.
6. **Generate the edited region.** Apply inpainting with context from the surrounding image, structural controls, and reference weights.
7. **Compare and approve.** Show before/after, side-by-side, overlay, version history, and send the approved result to the video workflow.

### **AI editing tools**

| Tool             | Expected behavior                                                 |
| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Smart Select     | Click a window, wall, roof, tree, floor, or furniture item        |
| Semantic Select  | Enter “select all glass windows”                                  |
| Annotation Brush | Paint an area and assign a text instruction                       |
| Reference Pin    | Attach a specific reference to a selected region                  |
| Material Replace | Change marble, wood, paint, tiles, or glass                       |
| Object Replace   | Replace furniture, vegetation, vehicles, decor                    |
| Add Object       | Insert objects with perspective and scale awareness               |
| Remove Object    | Remove an object and reconstruct the background                   |
| Geometry Lock    | Minimize changes to protected walls, openings, and rooflines      |
| Relight          | Change sun direction, artificial lighting, exposure, and ambience |
| Outpaint         | Extend the canvas beyond the original image boundaries            |

**Important technical requirement:** Geometry preservation is a constraint, not a guarantee. The system must provide a structural-difference preview and flag unintended architectural changes.

