The Video Studio converts approved still renders into architectural motion clips.

| Feature         | Requirements                                                 |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Input           | Single image, first/last frames, reference frames            |
| Camera movement | Dolly in/out, pan, tilt, orbit, crane, push-in               |
| Motion regions  | Trees, people, vehicles, water, curtains, clouds             |
| Duration        | 5–10-second clips initially; longer videos through stitching |
| Output          | MP4, WebM, configurable FPS and resolution                   |
| Consistency     | Architecture-lock mask, reference conditioning, frame checks |
| Timeline        | Clip ordering, transitions, trim, speed, keyframes           |
| Audio           | Optional ambience and licensed soundtrack integration        |

**Video generation acceptance criterion:** A user can take an approved still render, specify a slow camera movement, render a short clip, review temporal consistency, and export the result. Exact camera-path fidelity cannot be promised from single-image generative video; deterministic camera control requires a 3D scene or depth-aware rendering pipeline.

